{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/861495-blood-brothers-in-requiem-2e","id":861495,"title":"Blood Brothers in Requiem 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-07T18:35:51-07:00","id":861495,"title":"Blood Brothers in Requiem 2E","content":"Is there a Blood Brother equivalent (or port) from Masquerade? I'm not above making my own, but I figure I'd see if someone has made a copy or if I'm just missing the official version while digging through WoD Index.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:26:47-07:00","id":861534,"title":"","content":"What are Blood Brothers, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:49:29-07:00","id":861547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/861495-blood-brothers-in-requiem-2e?p=861534#post861534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Blood Brothers, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a bloodline from Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T20:02:32-07:00","id":861554,"title":"","content":"Seems like they would be some form of Promethean or golem or proto-vampire, as opposed to an actual bloodline.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Blood_Brothers\" target=\"_blank\">'They lack personal desires,' </a>would be a weird thing to play in Requiem.<br /> <br /> If someone's homebrewed it you would likely find it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/8627-requiem-homebrew-hub\">here.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-07-2016, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:15:06-07:00","id":861776,"title":"","content":"They might work with a bit of alteration. More like one vampire with five or so bodies. An independent hive mind, basically. Not sure if that's really viable as a PC though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:22:39-07:00","id":861783,"title":"","content":"The Danse Macabre has the Brethren of the Hundred Faces, which sort of mixes a hive mind with a pyramid scheme that was maybe slightly a bit like them, but the benefits of the hundred Faces really makes it a more ideal character option and they're capable of having personal ambition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T19:15:22-07:00","id":862357,"title":"","content":"There is the <b>Hive Nexus Gestalt</b> Devotion from the Carthian book (pg 194), which allows for a hive mind between several willing vampires with a number of other benefits, like improved intelligence, shared willpower, and bonuses to skills that at least one member is good with. I think the most direct way to translate the Blood Bros is to use this with maybe a Protean based Devotion to do the body-switching/addition weirdness. All the other details could be flavor for that Coterie-entity (they like sharing aspirations and they don't like nonconformity outside their group identity) or necessary compromises to make the whole thing work in the first place (if they're too dissimilar than the Devotion won't work). <br /> <br /> That said, I can't help but think of making a Blood Bros version based off of the Hive-Souled from Seers of the Throne, maybe as some kind of Super-Ghoul or even a Reverent level demi-vampire that requires its fellows to rise in power. I might have to write this up, along with the secondary devotion I mentioned before for the more vampire-oriented interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T19:44:48-07:00","id":862372,"title":"","content":"There's also the Carnival bloodline, with their The Show discipline. The fifth dot allows for a fusion with another vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:02:55-07:00","id":863015,"title":"","content":"The Neglatu bloodline might also possibly make for a good jumping off point, considering they're &quot;kinda&quot; Kindred and stick together, just like Blood Brothers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T06:23:15-07:00","id":864257,"title":"","content":"There's also the Barjot bloodline in the Carthians book, whose signature weakness is the can't stand to be removed from the company of their brood. If any one member of the group loses contact (visual, aural or tactile) with any member of the line, it must immediately make a Resolve + Composure roll. While they have no particular powers tied to psychic or physical fusion, i guess taking a look for potential ideas &amp; variants might still be useful anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:00:24-07:00","id":866894,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all of the suggestions! Lots of stuff to play with, there. I might spin out from the Carnival bloodline, that seems like a decent starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}